text:
clare: Found a small but annoying behavior on phone widths: opening the left nav slide-over causes the list header to shift down ~7px after animation finishes. Captured on iOS Safari and Chrome on Android. https://img.redwood.test/console/2026-04-header-shift.png

rui: Repro on Pixel emulator. Looks like when the overlay/backdrop is inserted we toggle body `overflow` and the sticky header recalculates. Sticky + transforms are brittle here.

ben: Quick idea: instead of sliding the sidebar over the content at <420px, use a bottom sheet for filters/columns only. Keep route nav in a compact dropdown in header. Bottom sheet won't interact with sticky header.

ava: Agree bottom sheet for filters. But we still need project switching. Could add a small project switcher chip in the header (left) that opens a focused modal for nav. That keeps header layout stable.

clare: Proposed breakpoints: <=400px bottom sheet for filter/columns; 401-720px full-screen modal for nav (position: fixed inset:0) so header isn't sticky; >720px keep slide-over. Thoughts?

rui: That sounds reasonable. CSS example I tried:```css
@media (max-width: 400px) {
  .filters-sheet { position: fixed; bottom: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 60vh; border-radius: 12px 12px 0 0; }
}
@media (min-width: 401px) and (max-width: 720px) {
  .sidebar-modal { position: fixed; inset: 0; }
  .main-header { position: static; }
}
```

ben: Accessibility notes: when using full-screen modal ensure focus trap and `aria-hidden` on main content. For bottom sheet use `role=dialog` and `aria-modal=true`. ESC and swipe-down must close. Also ensure the sheet doesn't prevent screen reader scroll.

ava: Hit target nit: compact rows currently have ~30px tappable height. We should make primary row target full width and >=44px tall. Secondary actions (kebab, copy) can be smaller but visually obvious. This reduces accidental taps.

clare: UX copy tweak: rename "Show columns" to "Columns & density" with helper text "Choose visible columns and row density (saved to device)". Makes it clearer it's persistent.

rui: Table truncation: long tokens (model IDs, URLs) are causing horizontal overflow in stacked layout. Solution: `word-break: break-word` + render as pill with ellipsis and small copy icon. On tap show full value in ephemeral toast with copy button. Also add `aria-label` on the copy button that reads the full value.

ben: For the A/B: Variant A stacked cards with full-row tap target; Variant B compact table with increased vertical padding to 44px. Run for 10 days, metrics: navigation success, kebab mis-taps, time-to-detail. I'll add flags.

ava: Search behavior: at <=480px hide inline search and show magnifier icon. When activated, present search as focused full-bleed input (role=search) so screen reader users get immediate context. Add `aria-label=\"Open search\"` to the icon.

design-bot: Reminder: if we change breakpoint tokens, update sources/design/tokens.md and add a note in sources/slack/product about the experiment.

clare: Action items: Rui - implement breakpoint tokens + modal/sheet CSS & ensure no header reflow; Ben - feature flag + A/B; Ava - a11y checklist + hit-target changes; Clare - update copy and schedule quick 6-person usability session. I'll post PR links and a short demo clip. Thanks! :thumbsup:
